1
00:00:01,220 --> 00:00:05,544
There's a planet out there as blue as Earth, and its weather would kill you in seconds.

2
00:00:05,614 --> 00:00:11,053
It's a gas giant about sixty-four light-years away, and its name is just a catalogue number.

3
00:00:11,123 --> 00:00:13,446
From far away, it would look a lot like home.

4
00:00:13,608 --> 00:00:15,456
A deep, azure blue.

5
00:00:15,526 --> 00:00:17,485
But that blue doesn't come from oceans.

6
00:00:17,555 --> 00:00:21,314
It hugs its star so tightly that a whole year there lasts just over two days.

7
00:00:21,384 --> 00:00:25,581
The side facing its star is around a thousand degrees Celsius.

8
00:00:25,651 --> 00:00:29,135
Winds rip around it at about seven thousand kilometres an hour.

9
00:00:29,363 --> 00:00:31,399
Nearly six times the speed of sound.

10
00:00:31,469 --> 00:00:36,145
And scientists think that blue may come from tiny drops of glass, floating in the air.

11
00:00:36,215 --> 00:00:38,071
Glass that may fall as rain.

12
00:00:38,326 --> 00:00:39,357
Sideways.

13
00:00:39,714 --> 00:00:41,777
So the next time you complain about the weather...

14
00:00:41,830 --> 00:00:43,500
at least it's not raining glass.
